{"qid":"Q30","names":["United States of America"],"title":"United States of America","endonym":{"native":"United States of America","lang":"en"},"capsule":"The United States declared independence from Britain in 1776, ratified its Constitution in 1788, and expanded westward through purchase (Louisiana, 1803; Alaska, 1867), treaty, and conquest to reach the Pacific by 1848 after the Mexican-American War. The Civil War (1861–1865) ended slavery and resolved the question of federal supremacy. By 1900 the country had become the world's largest industrial economy and acquired overseas territories in the Caribbean and Pacific following the Spanish-American War. It emerged from both World Wars as the pre-eminent global power, and the dissolution of the Soviet Union in 1991 left it the sole superpower within the attested span through 2024.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Territorial boundaries are extremely well documented by treaty, statute, and official survey; the contiguous 48 states have precisely known borders; only minor island possessions and tribal-land classifications carry any uncertainty.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: United States","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/United-States"},{"label":"Wikipedia: United States","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States"}],"britannica":"place/United-States","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"United States","rulers":[{"qid":"Q23","name":"George Washington","nativeName":"","roman":"","start":1789,"end":1797,"image":"Gilbert Stuart Williamstown Portrait of George Washington.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:File